# EOS Git and Release

## Canonical sources

- `.github/workflows/ci.yml` and `cd-release-gate.yml`
- `docs/releases/RELEASE_CAPABILITY_MATRIX.md`
- `docs/releases/EOS_FREEZE_GATE_STATUS.md`
- `DEPENDENCY_POLICY_L0.md`

## Git hygiene

- Work on a feature branch. Do not switch away from the assigned branch unless the human asks.
- One logical change per commit. Descriptive messages (e.g. `chore(cursor): …`).
- Never force-push. Never rewrite shared history. Never amend unless the human explicitly asks.
- Never commit secrets, `.env`, keys, tokens, or credential files.
- Do not delete files outside this workspace.

## Protected surfaces

- Do not merge pull requests (no `gh pr merge`, no merge commits to `main`) unless the human explicitly instructs it.
- Do not push to `main` directly.
- `Fundacion/` stays `Δ = 0` — no tracked or untracked writes.
- Do not tag production releases without PO sign-off.

## Release claims

- CI green on a subset is `PARTIALLY VERIFIED` at most.
- `PRODUCTION_READY` requires evidence across all required production dimensions and explicit PO authorization. Default: **NO**.
- Merge-to-main and live network/credentials are separate gates (`R-BOUNDARY-01`).
- Local fixture success is not production identity or production deploy proof.

## PRs

- Open a draft PR when asked to ship a change; mark ready only when tests for the change have been run.
- PR body: what changed, what was not touched (CORE / Fundacion), how it was verified.
- Do not enable auto-merge.

## Dependencies

L0 policy: Node built-ins only unless a recorded exception exists. Installing packages is medium/high risk — do not expand the supply chain on a rules or docs change.
